# Stories

A story is the unit of value this team finishes in one sprint: as a, I
want, so that, with story points, a rank, and acceptance criteria that
each name the test and the environment proving them. The agreed stories
not yet done, by rank, are the team's Product Backlog. A story is not a
unit of work. The issues that execute it are, and each one names the
story in an Implements line.

## Documents here

- Name: `stNNN-short-name.md`, numbered in order and never reused.
- Format: an SRD in the pinned parent release's Markdown format, with the fields docs/constitutions/design.md lists for this level; the draft skill drafts one in that layout.
- Status: `to_be_agreed` while it is drafted, `agreed` once it passes review, and `retired` when it is replaced. Only agreed documents are planned and rolled up. A retired document keeps its path, because links pin it.
- Parent: a feature or an epic.
- Changes go through an issue and the corpus gate, never a direct edit on main.

## What reads them

- The plan skill lists the Product Backlog with the team's velocity and writes the stories chosen at Sprint Planning onto the team's Sprint Goal.
- The sprint-end skill records the stories done at sprint end.
- Filing an issue checks the Implements line on the issues that execute a story.

See README.md at the repository's root for the whole hierarchy.
